    "narrative": "Our offensive core for today is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (67.97) and **Gleyber Torres** (67.52), who represent our highest-ceiling plays against favorable matchups. **Gleyber Torres** is particularly well-positioned leading off against the left-handed Kay; the combination of a strong park factor and a 13% boost from his SP matchup makes him a primary target for counting stats. Joining them in the \"Strong\" tier is **Brendan Donovan** (66.36) and **Jung Hoo Lee** (65.65). **Jung Hoo Lee** is a priority start not just for his expected efficiency against Lorenzen, but because his 85% sprint-speed correlation against a slower delivery provides a massive boost in our scarcest category, stolen bases. **Cal Raleigh** (62.77) also grades out as a must-start, as he enjoys a significant matchup advantage against the high-xERA Hayden Wesneski.\n\nThe most difficult decision of the day involved our bench, where **Luis Arraez** (47.52) narrowly missed the final lineup spot. While **Luis Arraez** provides a stable batting average floor, the optimizer prioritized the higher volatility and potential for multi-category production from **Lawrence Butler** (49.52), whose park factor boost in a hitter-friendly environment ultimately outweighed the consistency of the veteran. Elsewhere, we are closely monitoring the weather surrounding **JJ Bleday**, who remains on the bench with a 47.11 score due to a 40% rain risk and a negative platoon split.\n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the uncertainty of several lineup configurations. Both **Yainer Diaz** (43.83) and **Daulton Varsho** (55.69) are slated to face Emerson Hancock, but their sub-optimal projected batting positions keep their overall scores closer to our \"marginal\" floor than we would prefer. We are also keeping a close eye on **Bryce Harper** (60.06); while his xwOBA of .389 is elite, he is facing a left-handed matchup against Connor Prielipp that drags his base projection down slightly. Ensure all bench notifications are active, particularly for **Justin Crawford** and **Gavin Sheets**, should a last-minute lineup scratch open a path for a late-afternoon substitution.",
